Add duckdb_fetch_chunk_into: fetch into a caller-owned, reused data chunk

Companion to 0001 (both born from profiling C-API clients against
duckdb-python): duckdb_fetch_chunk allocates a fresh DataChunk per call —
MaterializedQueryResult::FetchInternal's DataChunk::Initialize was ~33% of a
chunk-streaming SELECT's runtime. duckdb_fetch_chunk_into scans the collection
directly into a caller-provided chunk instead:

  - MaterializedQueryResult::FetchInto(DataChunk&): FetchInternal minus the
    allocation, sharing the same scan cursor.
  - duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(result, chunk): C wrapper; for non-materialized
    results falls back to Fetch + DataChunk::Reference (correct, no alloc win).

Note for upstreaming: duckdb.h is autogenerated by scripts/generate_c_api.py;
this patch edits the generated header directly, an upstream PR must add the
definition to src/include/duckdb/main/capi/header_generation/ instead.

diff --git a/src/include/duckdb.h b/src/include/duckdb.h
index 8a18b4a..88e7f2c 100644
--- a/src/include/duckdb.h
+++ b/src/include/duckdb.h
@@ -5441,6 +5441,26 @@ It is not known beforehand how many chunks will be returned by this result.
 */
 DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_data_chunk duckdb_fetch_chunk(duckdb_result result);
 
+/*!
+Fetches the next data chunk from a duckdb_result into an existing data chunk, reusing its buffers instead of
+allocating a fresh chunk per call the way `duckdb_fetch_chunk` does. Call repeatedly until it returns false.
+
+The chunk must match the result's column types; create it with `duckdb_create_data_chunk` (or use a first chunk
+returned by `duckdb_fetch_chunk`). Each call overwrites the chunk's previous contents: consumers must copy what they
+need out of the chunk before fetching into it again. The caller keeps ownership of the chunk and must destroy it with
+`duckdb_destroy_data_chunk`.
+
+For materialized results this scans the underlying collection directly into the chunk (no per-fetch allocation); it
+shares the scan cursor with `duckdb_fetch_chunk`, so the two can be mixed. For other result types it is equivalent to
+`duckdb_fetch_chunk` plus referencing the fetched buffers.
+
+* @param result The result object to fetch the data chunk from.
+* @param chunk The data chunk to fetch into.
+* @return true if a chunk was fetched, false when the result is exhausted (or an error occurred — check
+`duckdb_result_error`).
+*/
+DUCKDB_C_API bool duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(duckdb_result result, duckdb_data_chunk chunk);
+
 //----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 // Cast Functions
 //----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
